ACE: Nice, and now...
ACE: Welcome to loops. Specifically, like I said before, the "while" loop.
ACE: It checks a condition, and as long as that condition is true, it keeps running the same code over and over.
Tyrone: So it's like an "if" statement that refuses to stop?
ACE: Exactly! But you have to be careful. If you don't change the variables inside the loop, it will run forever. We call that an infinite loop.
Tyrone: Sounds like a good way to crash my PC.
ACE: Don't worry, I won't let you. We also have the "do-while" loop, which guarantees the code runs at least once before checking the condition.
Tyrone: Run first, ask questions later.
ACE: Precisely. Let's see if you can keep the loops under control.
[end_timeline]